<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds closed little changed as the market awaited Tuesday's U.S. Federal Reserve policy-setting meeting.</p>
<p>Trading was also subdued due to the Pentecost holiday which kept some European markets, including Germany and France, closed.</p>
<p>Dealers were reluctant to take any major positions ahead of a possible hike in the U.S. fed funds rate by the Federal Open Market Committee on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The predominant impression is that the Fed may raise rates by 25 basis points,&quot; one analyst said.</p>
</text>
